Taller-than-16:9 display support (Vert+) for the game side of the native
renderer, next to upstream's ultrawide (Hor+) mode. The display-aspect
cvars get names that fit both directions:

  skate3_ultrawide                    -> skate3_match_display
  skate3_ultrawide_target_aspect      -> skate3_display_aspect (1.0 to 8.0)
  skate3_ultrawide_widen_game_frustum -> skate3_widen_game_frustum

The old names stay registered as deprecated. When settings.toml loads, an
old key is copied to its new name with a warning; if the new name is also
in the file (or set on the command line), the new name wins. Nothing else
reads the old names.

- skate3_app_common.cpp: drop the 16:9 floor on the target aspect; rename
  the cvars and migrate the deprecated ones.
- skate3_native_scene.cpp: scale clip.y of the published camera (Vert+).
- skate3_native_scene_gpu.cpp: letterbox the 16:9 2D stream (HUD, menus,
  FMV) and crop the photo grab to the same band.
- skate3_ultrawide_guest.h: widen the game's top/bottom cull planes
  (+5184/+5200) as well, under one shared lock. The old per-thread cache
  let concurrent cull workers re-widen planes already widened.
- config/skate3.example.toml: the new names.

